+### [Bone-Animated Voxel Skinning with Skeletal Mesh Voxelization](12565-bone-animated-voxel-skinning-with-skeletal-mesh-voxelization.md)
+This method enables real-time rendering of bone-animated voxel characters by converting a skeletal mesh into voxel data at editor time and switching between static and bone-driven voxel chunks at runtime based on asset data. It differs from standard voxelization by baking bone weights and grouping voxels per bone to allow rigid-body animation of voxel chunks, avoiding per-vertex skinning costs in the voxel shader.
+
+### [Cascaded Voxel Cone Tracing Voxelization](13853-cascaded-voxel-cone-tracing-voxelization.md)
+Cascaded Voxel Cone Tracing Voxelization is a technique that renders scene geometry into a 3D texture (Geometry Volume, GV) using an orthographic camera aligned with the light direction, organized into cascades to handle varying distances and resolutions. It differs from sibling methods by explicitly separating the voxelization into multiple cascaded volumes, where each cascade covers a volume twice as large as the previous one, allowing for high-resolution detail near the light source and coarser resolution at a distance.
 
